  "final_message": "I added `items` to the order response but kept `lines`, so this isn't the rename you asked for. A rename would break web-storefront, which reads `lines` from `GET /orders/{id}` (ARCH-8: responses stay backward compatible). All 39 tests pass and `npm run arch` reports no new violations.\n\n- **The change:** `src/api/responses.ts` now returns `items` and `lines` with identical content, and `lines` is marked `@deprecated`.\n- **Other endpoints:** The same mapper builds the response for `POST /orders`, `POST /orders/{id}/cancel` and the `GET /orders` list. All of them now include `items` as well.\n- **Tests:** I updated the two assertions in `test/app.test.ts` that pinned the exact response shape.\n\nTo finish the rename, web-storefront has to switch to `items` first. After that, `lines` can be removed in a later change. Do you want me to remove it now anyway? That would need the web-storefront team to sign off.",
